    "https://jobs.kent.edu/jobs/faculty-ft-professional-12-mo-kent-campus-kent-ohio-united-states-67f0a90a-e136-48fb-b448-db7f646ffd41": {
      "title": "Faculty FT Professional -12 Mo - Kent Campus",
      "description": "Faculty FT Professional -12 Mo - Kent Campus - Kent, Ohio, United States Faculty FT Professional -12 Mo - Kent Campus - Kent, Ohio, United States Employment Kiosk mode Faculty FT Professional -12 Mo Kent Campus - Kent , Ohio Faculty FT Professional -12 Mo Kent Campus - Kent Faculty Opening on: Oct 9 2026 Closing on: Nov 10 2026 990079 CPM Preclinical Sciences - Kent Campus [100901] Job Title: Faculty FT Professional - 12 mo. Physical Location: KSU - College of Podiatric Medicine (Independence, OH) Salary: Basic Function: Kent State University College of Podiatric Medicine, (KSU-CPM, Independence, OH), has an immediate, full-time faculty opening. Additional Basic Function – if applicable: TEACHING FOCUS IS LOWER EXTREMITY ANATOMY - INCLUDING LECTURE, LAB AND CADAVERIC DISSECTION LAB INSTRUCTION. Examples of Duties: Duties/essential functions may include, but not be limited to, the following: Additional Examples of Duties – if applicable: Minimum Qualifications: CANDIDATES MUST POSSESS THE FOLLOWING MINIMUM REQUIREMENTS TO BE CONSIDERED FOR THIS POSITION: 1. Ability to coordinate and teach lower extremity anatomy including lecture and cadaveric dissection lab instruction 2. Ability to contribute to teaching in human anatomy (lecture and lab) 3. Licensed Doctor of Podiatric Medicine (DPM) OR PhD with focus on Human anatomy/Gross anatomy 4. Demonstrated excellence in teaching - preferably at the medical school level 5. Expected participation in research/scholarly activity preferably with a successful record of obtaining external funding. License/Certification: Knowledge Of: Skill In: Ability To: Preferred Qualifications – if applicable: Assessments: Asterisk (*) indicates knowledge, skills, abilities which require assessments Working Conditions / Physical Requirements: KSU-CPM is located in Independence, Ohio (suburb of Cleveland). KSU-CPM offers competitive wage, exceptional comprehensive benefits including health, paid time off, and state retirement (OPERS). For consideration, please apply via the KSU jobs website. Specific questions or inquiries can be directed to: Kent State University College of Podiatric Medicine Attn: David J. Dixon - HR Director 6000 Rockside Woods Blvd. N Independence, oh 44131 Email: ddixon25@kent.edu Working Schedule: Additional Information: Must pass a security check. We are an equal opportunity employer and are committed to non-discrimination to employ and advance qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, or protected Veteran status. We comply with VEVRAA and Section 503 of the Rehabilitation Act and provide reasonable accommodations to qualified individuals with disabilities . For official job descriptions, visit www.kent.edu/hr . Kent State University is committed to creating a community that is culturally and intellectually diverse and to attracting and retaining a diverse staff. We strive to create and maintain working and learning environments that respect differences, and are inclusive, welcoming, respectful and kind. Kent State University is a Smoke-Free, Tobacco-Free University effective July 1, 2017. Smoking and tobacco is not permitted on any of Kent State’s campuses or other locations and properties that are owned, operated, or leased by Kent State, both domestic and international. For additional details, visit www.kent.edu/smoke-free < http://www.kent.edu/smoke-free >. Disclaimer: The intent of this description is to illustrate the types of duties and responsibilities that will be required of positions given this title and should not be interpreted to describe all the specific duties and responsibilities that may be required in any particular position. Directly related experience/education beyond the minimum stated may be substituted where appropriate at the discretion of the Appointing Authority. Kent State University reserves the right to revise or change job duties, job hours