    "https://jobs.kent.edu/jobs/faculty-tenure-track-9-mo-kent-campus-kent-ohio-united-states-f898f936-8d2a-48b3-a554-b17b08796012": {
      "title": "Faculty Tenure Track-9 Mo - Kent Campus",
      "description": "Faculty Tenure Track-9 Mo - Kent Campus - Kent, Ohio, United States Faculty Tenure Track-9 Mo - Kent Campus - Kent, Ohio, United States Employment Kiosk mode Faculty Tenure Track-9 Mo Kent Campus - Kent , Ohio Faculty Tenure Track-9 Mo Kent Campus - Kent Faculty Opening on: Oct 5 2026 Closing on: Nov 28 2026 986093 Interior Design Program - Kent Campus [101066] Job Title: Faculty Tenure Track-9 Mo Physical Location: Kent Campus - Kent, OH Salary: Basic Function: The College of Architecture and Environmental Design (CAED) at Kent State University invites applications for a tenure-track Assistant or Associate Professor of Interior Design . We seek a forward-thinking educator to teach design studios that integrate advanced technologies with human-centered design approaches while developing an innovative program of research, scholarship, and/or creative work. Candidates should demonstrate strong design capabilities and expertise in interior materials, methods, and construction practices; fabrication and making; and/or digital technologies. Additional Basic Function – if applicable: About CAED and Kent State: The CAED fosters integration of research and practice to address evolving environmental, societal, and technological challenges. The college is dedicated to advancing professional disciplines relating to the built environment and preparing graduates to lead in a rapidly changing world. Our programs engage in interdisciplinary collaboration across undergraduate offerings in Architecture, Interior Design, and Construction Management, graduate programs in Architecture, Healthcare Design, Urban Design, Landscape Architecture, Construction Management, and a research degree in Architecture and Environmental Design. Aligned university enterprises include Kent State’s highly ranked Fashion School, School of Visual Communication Design, College of the Arts, College of Aeronautics and Engineering, as well as the Advanced Materials and Environmental Science and Design Institutes and Design Innovation Hub dedicated to design education that addresses global challenges and transforms lives. The CIDA- and NASAD-accredited Interior Design Program provides a rigorous, high-quality education grounded in immersive studio experiences. We equip students with the skills, tools, and foundational design knowledge needed to become critical thinkers, innovative designers, and curious problem-solvers who expand the boundaries of the discipline while shaping human experience, well-being, and spatial equity in the built environment. In addition to a rich array of university assets, CAED resources include a design library branch, materials library, lighting lab, Fabrication Lab ), and the Robotically Augmented Design Lab (RadLAB). The CAED’s Cleveland Urban Design Collaborative (CUDC) provides an opportunity for community engagement dedicated to the betterment of our region. Substantial international study opportunities include sponsored studio/course travel opportunities, study-abroad programs in Florence and Paris, traveling workshops, and sponsored workshop, lecture, and exhibition series. The CAED's 38 full-time faculty and administrators and over 1300 undergraduate and graduate students occupy the LEED Platinum 107,000 sq. ft. John Elliot Center for Architecture and Design designed by Weiss/Manfredi; the newly renovated Beall Hall, Cleveland Urban Design Collaborative in downtown Cleveland; and the Palazzo Vettori in the historic center of Florence, Italy. Located midway between New York and Chicago in the Cleveland/Akron metro area, Kent State is an R1 research university in the heart of a burgeoning cultural and industrial region that is home to some of the world’s finest art museums, parks, universities, restaurants, theaters, music venues, and independent cinemas. These include the Cleveland Museum of Art, the Cleveland Orchestra, Playhouse Square, the Akron Art Museum designed by Coop Himmelb(l)au, and nearby landmarks such as Cuyahoga Valley National Park, the Cleveland Metroparks, Holden Arboretum, and Lake Erie's scenic shoreline. The area also features notable works by internationally recognized designers and architects, including James Corner, Frank Gehry, Farshid Moussavi, NADAAA, Laurie Olin, Stanley Saitowitz, and Rafael Viñoly, offering rich opportunities to engage with exemplary architecture, landscape architecture, urban design, and public space. For more information on Kent State see: http://www.kent.edu/ and the CAED at http://www.kent.edu/caed/. Examples of Duties: Duties/essential functions may include, but not be limited to, the following: The successful candidate will possess strong technical expertise and a demonstrated ability to teach and mentor students in a studio-based, hands-on learning environment that fosters experimentation, critical thinking, and creative problem-solving. They will be expected to integrate research, scholarship, and/or creative practice into their teaching while contributing to the continued advancement of the Interior Design program, the college, and the discipline. Teaching responsibilities may include foundational and/ or advanced interior design studios; digital applications; methods and materials; building systems and elective courses aligned with the candidate's research and/or creative expertise. Additional Examples of Duties – if applicable: Minimum Qualifications: The successful candidate must hold an advanced degree in Interior Design or related discipline and demonstrate teaching experience, professional/scholarly engagement, innovative research and/or creative design practice. Candidates should demonstrate a strong commitment to advancing the discipline of interior design and show promise for developing a national reputation through peer-reviewed scholarship/ research and/ or creative practice disseminated through leading venues Preferred Qualifications – if applicable: Assessments: Asterisk (*) indicates knowledge, skills, abilities which require assessments Working Conditions / Physical Requirements: Light work-Exerting up to 20 pounds of force occasionally, and/or up to 10 pounds of force frequently to move objects. Incumbent must be able to communicate with others. Incumbent may be required to travel from building to building frequently and off campus occasionally. Working Schedule: Additional Information: Application Process: Apply online at jobs.kent.edu (search by position 986093). Once you complete an online application, please attach: Letter of interest outlining vision for interior design education, a teaching philosophy, and research agenda. Curriculum Vitae Portfolio (Max 10MB) with research/scholarship, creative work, and teaching evidence (e.g., course syllabi and examples of student work) Contact information for three references Review begins September 1, 2026. Full consideration will be given to applicants who have submitted by October 30, 2026. For inquiries, contact Search Committee Chair Tina Patel at tpatel10@kent.edu. Must pass a security check. Kent State University is committed to creating a community that is culturally and intellectually diverse and to attracting and retaining a diverse staff. We strive to create and maintain working and learning environments that respect differences, and are inclusive, welcoming, respectful and kind. For official job descriptions, visit www.kent.edu/hr . Kent State University is a Smoke-Free, Tobacco-Free University effective July 1, 2017. Smoking and tobacco is not permitted on any of Kent State’s campuses or other locations and properties that are owned, operated, or leased by Kent State, both domestic and international. For additional details, visit www.kent.edu/smoke-free < http://www.kent.edu/smoke-free >. Disclaimer: The intent of this description is to illustrate the types of duties and responsibilities that will be required of positions given this title and should not be interpreted to describe all the specific duties and responsibilities that may be required in any particular position. Directly related experience/education beyond the minimum stated may be substituted where appropriate at the discretion of the Appointing Authority. Kent State University reserves the right to revise or change job duties, job hours, and responsibilities. Apply Now First Name (required) bb01b188 Last Name (required) a81b5362 Email (required) 6fd18fea Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Sign up for Job Alerts Job Alert 3c8b618f Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Employment Type Faculty Faculty Locations Kent Campus - Kent, Ohio, United States Kent Campus - Kent, Ohio, United States Home Organization/Dept. Interior Design Program - Kent Campus [101066] Interior Design Program - Kent Campus [101066] First Name (required) 751186e5 Last Name (required) e98374ad Email (required) e0d144d5 Submit Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Refer a Friend First Name (required) 16a2eb47 Last Name (required) db31d21e Email (required) 3d322f60 Referral 1de7ad55 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Other People Viewed Tutor - Intermittent 14111 Claridon Troy Road, Geauga Campus - Burton, Ohio, United States, 44021 The primary responsibility of the Nursing Tutor will be to provide support for the educational needs of nursing students at Kent State University Twinsburg Academic Center. Residential Dining Chef Kent Campus - Kent, Ohio, United States To manage culinary meals in residential dining facilities on Kent Campus. Residential dining encompasses two location feeding approximately 7,200 meals daily. Reports to Campus Executive Chef, or designated supervisor. Food Service Worker I -INTERNAL ONLY OPENING FOR CURRENT KSU AFSCME EMPLOYEES ONLY Kent Campus - Kent, Ohio, United States Assists in food preparation and