      "description": "Faculty Non-Tenure Track-9 Mo - Ashtabula Campus - Ashtabula, Ohio, United States Faculty Non-Tenure Track-9 Mo - Ashtabula Campus - Ashtabula, Ohio, United States Employment Kiosk mode Faculty Non-Tenure Track-9 Mo Ashtabula Campus - Ashtabula , Ohio Faculty Non-Tenure Track-9 Mo Ashtabula Campus - Ashtabula Faculty Opening on: Aug 10 2026 Closing on: Nov 15 2026 991393 CATS-Rad Tech/CT/MRI/Mammography - Ashtabula Campus [200099] Job Title: Faculty Non-Tenure Track-9 Mo Physical Location: Ashtabula Campus - Ashtabula, OH Salary: Basic Function: Kent State University at Ashtabula seeks candidates for full-time, non-tenure track faculty position to teach in a JRCERT Accredited Associate Degree Program in Radiologic Technology. Additional Basic Function – if applicable: Examples of Duties: Duties/essential functions may include, but not be limited to, the following: Additional Examples of Duties – if applicable: Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor's degree in a relevant field. Two years of Radiologic clinical experience. Proficient in course development, instruction, evaluation, and academic advising. One year experience as an instructor in a JRCERT accredited program. Holds current American Registry of Radiologic Technologists (ARRT), certification and registration in Radiologic Technology. Preferred Qualifications – if applicable: Assessments: Asterisk (*) indicates knowledge, skills, abilities which require assessments Working Conditions / Physical Requirements: Light work-Exerting up to 20 pounds of force occasionally, and/or up to 10 pounds of force frequently to move objects. Incumbent must be able to communicate with others. Incumbent may be required to travel from building to building frequently and off campus occasionally. Working Schedule: Additional Information: TO APPLY FOR THIS OPENING, PLEASE SUBMIT AN ONLINE APPLICATION AND THEN ATTACH A LETTER OF APPLICATION EXPRESSING INTEREST REFERENCING THE POSITION NUMBER, A CURRENT CURRICULUM VITAE, AND CONTACT INFORMATION FOR 3 PROFESSIONAL REFERENCES. PLEASE FORWARD YOUR TRANSCRIPTS TO JRSAKSA@KENT.EDU Must pass a security check. Kent State University is committed to creating a community that is culturally and intellectually diverse and to attracting and retaining a diverse staff. We strive to create and maintain working and learning environments that respect differences, and are inclusive, welcoming, respectful and kind. For official job descriptions, visit www.kent.edu/hr . Kent State University is a Smoke-Free, Tobacco-Free University effective July 1, 2017. Smoking and tobacco is not permitted on any of Kent State’s campuses or other locations and properties that are owned, operated, or leased by Kent State, both domestic and international. For additional details, visit www.kent.edu/smoke-free < http://www.kent.edu/smoke-free >. Disclaimer: The intent of this description is to illustrate the types of duties and responsibilities that will be required of positions given this title and should not be interpreted to describe all the specific duties and responsibilities that may be required in any particular position. Directly related experience/education beyond the minimum stated may be substituted where appropriate at the discretion of the Appointing Authority. Kent State University reserves the right to revise or change job duties, job hours, and responsibilities. Apply Now First Name (required) 3a606d83 Last Name (required) 1dc11394 Email (required) 1a65d105 Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Sign up for Job Alerts Job Alert 77bd4a73 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Employment Type Faculty Faculty Locations Ashtabula Campus - Ashtabula, Ohio, United States Ashtabula Campus - Ashtabula, Ohio, United States Home Organization/Dept. CATS-Rad Tech/CT/