    "https://jobs.kent.edu/jobs/faculty-non-tenure-track-9-mo-assistant-professor-management-kent-campus-kent-ohio-united-states-1b554cee-e991-4805-b132-72dc44387bd8": {
      "title": "Faculty Non-Tenure Track-9 Mo - Assistant Professor, Management - Kent Campus",
      "description": "Faculty Non-Tenure Track-9 Mo - Assistant Professor, Management - Kent Campus - Kent, Ohio, United States Faculty Non-Tenure Track-9 Mo - Assistant Professor, Management - Kent Campus - Kent, Ohio, United States Employment Kiosk mode Faculty Non-Tenure Track-9 Mo - Assistant Professor, Management Kent Campus - Kent , Ohio Faculty Non-Tenure Track-9 Mo - Assistant Professor, Management Kent Campus - Kent Faculty Opening on: Jul 23 2026 Closing on: Oct 31 2026 998744 Management - Kent Campus [101327] Job Title: Faculty Non-Tenure Track-9 Mo Physical Location: Kent Campus - Kent, Ohio Salary: Basic Function: The Department of Management within the Ambassador Crawford College of Business and Entrepreneurship at Kent State University seeks qualified candidates to apply for a non-tenure-track position in Management effective Fall 2027 with a start date of August 19, 2027. Additional Basic Function – if applicable: Examples of Duties: Duties/essential functions may include, but not be limited to, the following: The candidate will primarily teach courses in Human Resource Management (e.g., HRM, HR Analytics and ERP Analytics, Staffing, Global HR) as well as Organizational Behavior and other management courses such as Advanced Professional Development, and Organizational Mentoring, as needed and depending on the qualifications of the candidate. Additional Examples of Duties – if applicable: Minimum Qualifications: Candidates with a PhD or DBA degree in business or management with a concentration in human resource management, organizational behavior, or equivalent terminal degree in the management field. For candidates with a doctoral degree earned prior to May 2023, evidence of recent professional activities that allow them to maintain currency in the field is required. All-But-Dissertation (ABD) doctoral students are also encouraged to apply if they are highly likely to earn their terminal degree before Fall 2027. Preferred Qualifications – if applicable: In addition, evidence of effective teaching is preferred but not required. Assessments: Asterisk (*) indicates knowledge, skills, abilities which require assessments Working Conditions / Physical Requirements: Light work-Exerting up to 20 pounds of force occasionally, and/or up to 10 pounds of force frequently to move objects. Incumbent must be able to communicate with others. Incumbent may be required to travel from building to building frequently and off campus occasionally. Working Schedule: Additional Information: Value Statement Kent State University is committed to creating a community that is culturally and intellectually diverse and to attracting and retaining a diverse staff. We strive to create and maintain working and learning environments that respect differences, and are inclusive, welcoming, respectful and kind. Must pass a security check. We are an equal opportunity employer and all qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, national origin, disability status, protected veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by law. For official job descriptions, visit www.kent.edu/hr . Kent State University is a Smoke-Free, Tobacco-Free University effective July 1, 2017. Smoking and tobacco is not permitted on any of Kent State’s campuses or other locations and properties that are owned, operated, or leased by Kent State, both domestic and international. For additional details, visit www.kent.edu/smoke-free < http://www.kent.edu/smoke-free >. Review of applications will begin on October 1, 2026, and continue until the position is filled. Please submit a cover letter, curriculum vitae or resume, evidence of teaching effectiveness (if available), and the contact information of three references. To receive full consideration, submit the application materials described above by October 31, 2026 , for job number 998744 at https://jobs.kent.edu. Qualified applicants may be asked to provide additional application materials. Any questions about this position can be addressed to the Department Chair, Prof. Asli Arikan at aarikan@kent.edu. Disclaimer: The intent of this description is to illustrate the types of duties and responsibilities that will be required of positions given this title and should not be interpreted to describe all the specific duties and responsibilities that may be required in any particular position. Directly related experience/education beyond the minimum stated may be substituted where appropriate at the discretion of the Appointing Authority. Kent State University reserves the right to revise or change job duties, job hours, and responsibilities. Apply Now First Name (required) eb799bae Last Name (required) 6b1e6ce2 Email (required) cd5bf85f Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Sign up for Job Alerts Job Alert 73b5384d Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Employment Type Faculty Faculty Locations Kent Campus - Kent, Ohio, United States Kent Campus - Kent, Ohio, United States Home Organization/Dept. Management - Kent Campus [101327] Management - Kent Campus [101327] First Name (required) dda7a1a5 Last Name (required) bad21168 Email (required) c1378934 Submit Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Refer a Friend First Name (required) 3dfbbac3 Last Name (required) 8bb1a41f Email (required) 137e073f Referral b3a42d24 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Other People Viewed Tutor - Intermittent 14111 Claridon Troy Road, Geauga Campus - Burton, Ohio, United States, 44021 The primary responsibility of the Nursing Tutor will be to provide support for the educational needs of nursing students at Kent State University Twinsburg Academic Center. Residential Dining Chef Kent Campus - Kent, Ohio, United States To manage culinary meals in residential dining facilities on Kent Campus. Residential dining encompasses two location feeding approximately 7,200 meals daily. Reports to Campus Executive Chef, or designated supervisor. Food Service Worker I -INTERNAL ONLY OPENING FOR CURRENT KSU AFSCME EMPLOYEES ONLY Kent Campus - Kent, Ohio, United States Assists in food preparation and related food service activities. Reports to Food Service Manager, Food Service General Manager, or other designated supervisor. Cook I - INTERNAL ONLY OPENING FOR CURRENT KSU AFSCME EMPLOYEES ONLY Kent Campus - Kent, Ohio, United States Cooks foods in production quantities. Reports to Food Service Manager, Food Service General Manager, or other designated supervisor. Food Service Worker I -INTERNAL ONLY OPENING FOR CURRENT KSU AFSCME EMPLOYEES ONLY Kent Campus - Kent, Ohio, United States Assists in food preparation and related food service activities. Reports to Food Service Manager, Food Service General Manager, or other designated supervisor. Career Advisor Kent Campus - Kent, Ohio, United States To provide comprehensive career support and develop career related resources for students, alumni, and other constituencies. This position will be a liaison for multiple specific student populations. Reports to designated supervisor. Apply Now First Name (required) 6d6ccceb Last Name (required) 6d31e62c Email (required) c0337d43 Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Before you soar away, Join our talent community! First Name (required) 0d88ca7e Last Name (required) 79447273 Email (required) 75844e4f Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you for Joining Our Talent Community Close Candidate Details This website uses cookies. We use cookies to personalize content such as job recommendations, and to analyze our traffic. You consent to our cookies if you click \"I Accept\". If you click on \"I Do Not Accept\", then we will not use cookies but you may have a deteriorated user experience. You can change your settings by clicking on the Settings link on the top right of the device. I do not accept I accept Please choose a home organization/dept."
